elif nav_selection == "🛡️ Detection Rules":

    st.markdown("<div class='soc-panel-title'>🛡️ DETECTION ENGINE RULES & SYSTEM WORKFLOW</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    st.markdown(
        "<div style='color: #94A3B8; font-size: 0.88rem; margin-bottom: 20px;'>The analyzer parses authentication logs, normalizes heterogeneous events, applies rule-based threat detection logic, and persists alerts into SQLite.</div>",
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    # Visual System Workflow
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="soc-panel-title">🔄 END-TO-END SYSTEM WORKFLOW PIPELINE</div>
        <div class="wf-step-container">
            <div class="wf-step-card">
                <div class="wf-step-num">STAGE 01</div>
                <div class="wf-step-title">Log Ingestion & Detection</div>
                <div class="wf-step-desc">Accepts multi-file uploads (.csv, .log, .txt). Inspects file headers to identify Windows CSV, Event Viewer Text, SSH Syslog, or Pipe-delimited logs.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-step-card">
                <div class="wf-step-num">STAGE 02</div>
                <div class="wf-step-title">Extraction & Normalization</div>
                <div class="wf-step-desc">Extracts timestamp, event type, username, IP (IPv4/IPv6), port, and status. Normalizes heterogeneous records into a unified Python dictionary schema.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-step-card">
                <div class="wf-step-num">STAGE 03</div>
                <div class="wf-step-title">Detection Rule Engine</div>
                <div class="wf-step-desc">Evaluates normalized events against rule criteria: Brute-Force (≥3 failed from IP) and Multiple-Account spray (≥3 distinct failed usernames from IP).</div>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-step-card">
                <div class="wf-step-num">STAGE 04</div>
                <div class="wf-step-title">Severity & Risk Scoring</div>
                <div class="wf-step-desc">Assigns severity classifications (HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW) and calibrated risk scores (70/100 for brute-force, 50/100 for account spraying).</div>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-step-card">
                <div class="wf-step-num">STAGE 05</div>
                <div class="wf-step-title">Persistent SQLite Storage</div>
                <div class="wf-step-desc">Stores newly generated alerts in security_alerts.db table, executing deduplication checks to prevent duplicate alerts from re-analysis.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="wf-step-card">
                <div class="wf-step-num">STAGE 06</div>
                <div class="wf-step-title">SOC Analytics & Reporting</div>
                <div class="wf-step-desc">Renders interactive timelines, severity donuts, top IP charts, searchable alert tables, and generates CSV/JSON audit exports.</div>
            </div>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    st.markdown("<hr style='border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.1); margin: 20px 0;'>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    st.markdown("<div class='soc-panel-title'>⚙️ ACTIVE DETECTION RULES</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)

    # Rule 1: Brute-Force
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="rule-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #EF4444;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <div>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #38BDF8; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-weight: 700;">SEC-RUL-001</span>
                    <div style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #F8FAFC; margin-top: 2px;">Brute-Force Authentication Attack</div>
                </div>
                <span class="sev-badge sev-high">HIGH</span>
            </div>
            <div style="color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 0.84rem; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.6;">
                <strong>What it detects:</strong> Repeated failed authentication attempts from a single source IP address, indicating a possible password guessing attack.<br><br>
                <strong>Conditions:</strong> ≥ 3 failed login events originating from the same IP address.<br><br>
                <strong>Severity:</strong> HIGH &nbsp; | &nbsp; <strong>Risk Score:</strong> 70 / 100<br><br>
                <strong>Limitations:</strong> This rule counts total failed attempts across the entire uploaded log file without a time window. A slow brute-force attack spanning multiple days would still trigger the alert if 3+ failures exist in the same file. The threshold of 3 is conservative and may generate false positives in environments with frequent legitimate failures.<br><br>
                <strong>Example:</strong> An attacker at IP 192.168.1.105 sends 5 failed login attempts for user "administrator" — all 5 fail → alert triggered with count=5.
            </div>
            <div style="background: rgba(11, 18, 32, 0.6); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.78rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
                <span style="color: #94A3B8;">Threshold: <strong style="color: #F8FAFC;">≥ 3 failed attempts from single IP</strong></span>
                <span style="color: #4ADE80; font-weight: 600;">● Active (Implemented)</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    # Rule 2: Multiple-Account
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="rule-card" style="border-left: 4px solid #F59E0B;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <div>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.7rem; color: #38BDF8; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-weight: 700;">SEC-RUL-002</span>
                    <div style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #F8FAFC; margin-top: 2px;">Multiple-Account Password Spraying</div>
                </div>
                <span class="sev-badge sev-medium">MEDIUM</span>
            </div>
            <div style="color: #CBD5E1; font-size: 0.84rem; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.6;">
                <strong>What it detects:</strong> A single source IP failing authentication against multiple different usernames, indicating credential spraying where an attacker tests common passwords across many accounts.<br><br>
                <strong>Conditions:</strong> ≥ 3 distinct usernames with failed login attempts from the same IP address.<br><br>
                <strong>Severity:</strong> MEDIUM &nbsp; | &nbsp; <strong>Risk Score:</strong> 50 / 100<br><br>
                <strong>Limitations:</strong> Only counts distinct usernames from failed events. If a legitimate user mistypes credentials for different service accounts, it could trigger a false positive. Events with username "UNKNOWN" are excluded from this count.<br><br>
                <strong>Example:</strong> IP 10.0.0.99 fails login for users "root", "admin", "guest" → 3 distinct usernames → alert triggered.
            </div>
            <div style="background: rgba(11, 18, 32, 0.6); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.78rem; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
                <span style="color: #94A3B8;">Threshold: <strong style="color: #F8FAFC;">≥ 3 distinct usernames failed from single IP</strong></span>
                <span style="color: #4ADE80; font-weight: 600;">● Active (Implemented)</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    # Future enhancements
    st.markdown("<div class='soc-panel-title' style='margin-top: 20px;'>🔮 Planned Future Enhancements</div>", unsafe_allow_html=True)
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="info-box" style="border-left: 3px solid #6366F1;">
            The following detection rules are <strong>not yet implemented</strong> and are planned for future development:
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Time-Window Brute-Force:</strong> Detect N failed attempts within a configurable time window (e.g., 5 failures in 60 seconds).</li>
                <li><strong>Geographic Anomaly:</strong> Flag logins from unusual geographic locations using IP geolocation.</li>
                <li><strong>Impossible Travel:</strong> Detect logins from geographically distant locations within a short time frame.</li>
                <li><strong>Privilege Escalation:</strong> Detect sequences where a failed login is immediately followed by a successful one.</li>
                <li><strong>MITRE ATT&CK Mapping:</strong> Map detections to specific ATT&CK techniques for threat classification.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )


