                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #94A3B8; font-weight: 600;">Log Parsing</td>
                    <td style="padding: 8px 12px; color: #F8FAFC;">Python <code>re</code> (regex) + <code>csv</code> modules</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    # E. Supported Log Sources
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="info-box">
            <h3>E. Supported Log Sources</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Windows Security CSV:</strong> CSV files with headers like <code>EventID</code>, <code>SourceIP</code>, <code>LogonType</code>. Parses Event IDs 4624 (Success) and 4625 (Failed).</li>
                <li><strong>Windows Event Viewer Text:</strong> Text blocks containing <code>TimeCreated</code>, <code>Id</code>, <code>Account Name</code>, <code>Source Network Address</code> fields.</li>
                <li><strong>Linux / Kali SSH Syslog:</strong> Standard syslog format with <code>sshd</code> messages. Extracts usernames, IPs (including IPv6 <code>::1</code>), and authentication status.</li>
                <li><strong>Pipe-Delimited Auth Log:</strong> Simple format: <code>timestamp | event | username | ip | status</code></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    # F. Limitations
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="info-box">
            <h3>F. Limitations</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Detection quality depends on the supported log formats and available fields in the uploaded files.</li>
                <li>The system analyzes <strong>uploaded log files</strong> — it does not perform continuous real-time monitoring.</li>
                <li>Detection rules use simple threshold-based counting without time-window analysis.</li>
                <li>The brute-force threshold of 3 is conservative and may cause false positives in busy environments.</li>
                <li>IP geolocation and threat intelligence enrichment are not implemented.</li>
                <li>The parser may not recognize all possible syslog or Windows log variations.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )

    # G. Future Enhancements
    st.markdown(
        """
        <div class="info-box">
            <h3>G. Future Enhancements</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Additional log format support (Apache, Nginx, Firewall logs)</li>
                <li>Time-window based detection (e.g., N failures within M seconds)</li>
                <li>Threat intelligence integration for IP reputation lookup</li>
                <li>MITRE ATT&CK technique mapping for alert classification</li>
                <li>Machine learning-based anomaly detection</li>
                <li>Email/Slack notifications for high-severity alerts</li>
                <li>Real-time log monitoring via file watching or syslog ingestion</li>
                <li>User authentication and role-based access control</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="color: #64748B; font-style: italic; font-size: 0.82rem;">
                The above items are planned improvements and are not currently implemented.
            </p>
        </div>
        """,
        unsafe_allow_html=True
    )


